---
title: GNeck — Learn every note on the guitar neck by shape
description: GNeck teaches you every note on the guitar fretboard by learning one shape instead of 78 note names. For iPhone and iPad. Coming soon to the App Store.
---
{%- set isLive = appStoreUrl and not appStoreUrl.startsWith('[') %}

<section class="gn-hero">
  <div class="gn-wrap">
    <img class="gn-icon" src="/assets/gneck/icon.webp" alt="GNeck app icon" width="512" height="512" fetchpriority="high">
    <h1>GNeck</h1>
    <p class="gn-tagline">See the neck. Remember the shape. Know where every note lives.</p>
    <div class="gn-cta">
      {%- if isLive %}
      {#- Replace this button with Apple's official "Download on the App Store" badge artwork, unmodified, once the app is live. -#}
      <a class="gn-button" href="{{ appStoreUrl }}">View on the App Store</a>
      {%- else %}
      <span class="gn-soon">Coming soon to the App Store</span>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    <p class="gn-platforms">For iPhone and iPad · iOS 17 or later</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gn-section" id="how-it-works" style="border-top:0;padding-top:40px">
  <div class="gn-wrap">
    <div class="gn-pair">
      <figure class="gn-figure">
        <img class="gn-shot" src="/assets/gneck/01-look.webp" alt="Every G on a guitar neck lit up in amber and connected into a zig-zag shape" width="1500" height="689">
        <figcaption>Glimpse the shape.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="gn-figure">
        <img class="gn-shot" src="/assets/gneck/02-recall.webp" alt="A guitar neck with four G notes found and one wrong tap marked as A" width="1500" height="689" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>Then tap it from memory.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="gn-steps">
      <div class="gn-step">
        <span class="gn-step-num">1</span>
        <h3>Look</h3>
        <p>A note's whole constellation lights up and connects into the Master Shape.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gn-step">
        <span class="gn-step-num">2</span>
        <h3>Hide</h3>
        <p>It disappears.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gn-step">
        <span class="gn-step-num">3</span>
        <h3>Recall</h3>
        <p>You tap every position from memory. Right taps glow amber. A wrong tap quietly shows you which note it really was.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="gn-note" style="margin-top:0">No quizzes, no multiple choice. Pulling a shape out of memory is what makes it stick.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gn-section">
  <div class="gn-wrap gn-center">
    <h2 class="gn-big">One shape. Twelve slides.<br><span>Every note.</span></h2>
    <p class="gn-lede">Most fretboard apps make you memorize note names one at a time. GNeck works the way your memory does. You remember patterns and places far better than lists. Learn the shape once, slide it, done.</p>
    <figure class="gn-figure" style="margin-top:56px">
      <img class="gn-shot" src="/assets/gneck/03-explore.webp" alt="Explore screen showing the G shape and a picker for all twelve notes" width="1500" height="689" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>Slide one shape to every note.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gn-section">
  <div class="gn-wrap gn-center">
    <p class="gn-eyebrow">Daily practice</p>
    <h2 class="gn-h2">Five minutes a day.</h2>
    <p class="gn-lede">One button builds today's 8 to 12 rounds. Each note comes back right before you'd forget it. Ten short units take you from the open strings to the whole neck.</p>
    <div class="gn-duo">
      <figure class="gn-figure">
        <img class="gn-shot" src="/assets/gneck/04-home.webp" alt="Home screen with the Daily Neck button and a progress card" width="689" height="1500" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>Five minutes a day.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="gn-figure">
        <img class="gn-shot" src="/assets/gneck/05-learn.webp" alt="Learning path of ten units, four completed" width="689" height="1500" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>Ten short steps to the whole neck.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gn-section">
  <div class="gn-wrap">
    <div class="gn-center">
      <p class="gn-eyebrow">What's inside</p>
      <h2 class="gn-h2">Built by a guitarist, for guitarists.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="gn-features">
      <div class="gn-feature">
        <span class="gn-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>A path that fades the training wheels</h3>
        <p>Each note moves on its own through five stages: trace a faint guide, glimpse the full shape, see just the first note, see only the name, then beat the clock.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gn-feature">
        <span class="gn-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Ten short units</h3>
        <p>Anchors, Octave Shapes, the Master Shape, slides to A, D, G and B, F and C, Sharps &amp; Flats, Full Neck. Every lesson is three quick visual steps, then straight to playing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gn-feature">
        <span class="gn-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Daily Neck</h3>
        <p>One button builds today's 8 to 12 rounds, about five minutes. It brings each note back right before you'd forget it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gn-feature">
        <span class="gn-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Explore</h3>
        <p>A free neck. Tap any fret to hear it and see its name, hold a note to see its octave, or pick any note and watch the Master Shape slide across the neck to it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gn-feature">
        <span class="gn-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Made for guitarists</h3>
        <p>A real-looking neck in rosewood, nickel and bronze, with a gentle plucked-string sound on every note. Standard, Drop D, Drop C and 7-string tunings, each with its own progress. Left-handed and flipped layouts. ♯ or ♭ names.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gn-feature">
        <span class="gn-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Accessible</h3>
        <p>VoiceOver, with a dedicated way to play rounds by ear and touch. Dynamic Type, Reduce Motion, and nothing that relies on color alone.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="gn-note">Built on well-studied learning techniques like retrieval practice and spaced repetition.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gn-section">
  <div class="gn-wrap">
    <div class="gn-split">
      <div>
        <p class="gn-eyebrow">Progress</p>
        <h2 class="gn-h2">Watch the whole neck light up.</h2>
        <p class="gn-lede">A full-neck heatmap glows from dim to amber to green as you master each note. No streaks to break, no badges, no nagging.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="gn-figure gn-portrait">
        <img class="gn-shot" src="/assets/gneck/06-progress.webp" alt="Progress screen with a heatmap of mastered notes on the neck" width="689" height="1500" loading="lazy">
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gn-section" id="privacy">
  <div class="gn-wrap">
    <div class="gn-privacy">
      <p class="gn-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h2 class="gn-h2">Your practice stays yours.</h2>
      <ul class="gn-nos">
        <li>No account</li>
        <li>No ads</li>
        <li>No tracking</li>
        <li>No in-app purchases</li>
        <li>Works completely offline</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="gn-lede">GNeck never collects any data. Its App Store privacy label is <span class="gn-label">Data Not Collected</span>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gn-section gn-final" style="border-top:0;padding-top:24px">
  <div class="gn-wrap">
    <img class="gn-icon" src="/assets/gneck/icon.webp" alt="" width="512" height="512" loading="lazy">
    <h2 class="gn-h2">One shape. Every note.</h2>
    <div class="gn-cta" style="margin-top:24px">
      {%- if isLive %}
      <a class="gn-button" href="{{ appStoreUrl }}">View on the App Store</a>
      {%- else %}
      <span class="gn-soon">Coming soon to the App Store</span>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    <p class="gn-platforms">For iPhone and iPad · iOS 17 or later</p>
    <p class="gn-applinks">
      <a href="/apps/gneck/support/">Support</a>
      <a href="/apps/gneck/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>
    </p>
    <p class="gn-applegal">Apple, the Apple logo, iPhone, iPad and App Store are trademarks of Apple Inc., registered in the U.S. and other countries.</p>
  </div>
</section>
